From 50ea08776484db29383d649733e8a1f7e433efa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bizuayeu <30091157+Bizuayeu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:57:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 22/39] GLM-5.3-Flash on CUDA: a decode window's DSA index
 scores on glm_index_scores (TF_GLM_DSCORES)

MiaAI-Lab's patch 0091 (attn5-0070-glm-decode-index-scores-on-glm-index-scores,
in MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104 0049d7c, Apache-2.0), moved onto the
decode select (TF_GLM_DSEL). A decode window under rows_from rows, of 8 rows or
more (or 4 from 2,048 64-pool blocks) on an aligned key cache, takes
tf_glm_index_scores (8 rows a CTA, each key tile staged once for the window's
rows, decodeLoop tiles a CTA) instead of tf_glm_scores (a CTA a row and block);
the kernel writes tf_glm_scores' bytes. Prompt chunks keep TF_GLM_INDEX_CUDA's
rule and one-row windows keep tf_glm_scores. glm_index's scores load unless
TF_GLM_DSCORES=0, a glm row of platform/environment.zig (a flag, default on)
with its docs/environment.md row, read as TF_GLM_DSEL is; the comments are one
line each. glm-index-check's decode section runs selectTokens with the decode
scores in the new set.
